>
  <section>
    <p>UAE card, bank and loyalty-programme terms are often spread across product pages, key-facts statements, schedules of charges and campaign terms. A product page may describe the headline benefit while a separate document sets the fee, eligibility rule, cap or expiry.</p>
    <p>DubaiPoints exists to bring those details into one editorial record without giving a summary more force than its sources support. Figures are shown in the unit the provider publishes, with AED used for monetary comparisons where the evidence permits it. Verification dates show when an entry was checked; they are not a promise that a provider has made no later change.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the publication is for</h2>
    <p>DubaiPoints is an editorial publication, not a personalised recommendation service or a complete comparison engine. It covers the products and offers the editorial team has been able to evidence, and it leaves unresolved fields out or marks them for review.</p>
    <p>The working products are card and programme reviews, a salary-transfer tracker, dated deals, practical guides and AED valuation methodology. Each has a different evidence boundary: a tracker records what was found at a stated check date; an analysis explains its assumptions; a recommendation must disclose the basis for the judgement.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the publication does not claim</h2>
    <p>Coverage is not complete, inclusion is not endorsement and a missing product is not a negative verdict. DubaiPoints does not provide personalised financial, legal, tax or immigration advice.</p>
    <p>Commercial relationships may not determine rankings or editorial verdicts. Any monetised link must be disclosed where it appears and governed by the <a href="/how-we-make-money/">how-we-make-money policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to hold DubaiPoints to its standard</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:info@dubaipoints.ae">info@dubaipoints.ae</a> when a figure is wrong, a source no longer supports a claim, or two pages contradict each other.</p>
    <p>Material corrections are recorded in the <a href="/corrections/">corrections log</a>. The <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> sets the verification standard, and the <a href="/how-we-make-money/">how-we-make-money policy</a> sets the commercial boundary.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p>Dubai, August 2026.</p>
  </section>

